Ranger uses multiple licenses.

Ranger-authored source code outside the gallery/ directory is licensed
under the MIT License, unless a file or subdirectory explicitly states
otherwise. See LICENSE-MIT. This includes the compiler, the runtime,
lib/ — and with it the image codecs (lib/image). The EVG layout engine
lives in terotests/evg (MIT); this tree fetches it to deps/evg. Both
moved out of gallery/ and to MIT in September 2026.

Ranger-authored source code under gallery/ is licensed under the GNU
Affero General Public License version 3 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later),
unless a file or subdirectory explicitly states otherwise.
See LICENSE-AGPL-3.0 and gallery/LICENSE.

Third-party components remain subject to their respective licenses.

Ranger does not impose a license on programs compiled with Ranger. The
license of generated output follows the source code and other
components from which that output is derived. Compiled or transpiled
forms of AGPL-licensed Gallery programs remain covered by the AGPL.

Alternative commercial licenses may be available for components under
gallery/.

SPDX identifiers:

  MIT                 — files outside gallery/ (unless otherwise stated)
  AGPL-3.0-or-later   — files under gallery/ (unless otherwise stated)

Further notes, dependency rules, and third-party exceptions:
see LICENSING.md.
